   "date": "2014-07-03T07:47:06Z",
   "subject": "Re: error messages re: inversion of covariance, logl.H1, and factors with more than 2 levels",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On 07/02/2014 07:55 PM, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rachael...@gmail.com</a> wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hi,\r<br>&gt; As a last resort, I hope someone in this group will be able to shed some\r<br>&gt; light on issues I&#39;ve been having while trying to build/run a SEM using\r<br>&gt; lavaan.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; The problem: lavaan keeps throwing more and more errors including...\r<br>\r<br>&gt; -------------------------\r<br>&gt; Warning message: In lav_samplestats_from_data(lavdata = lavdata, missing\r<br>&gt; = lavoptions$missing, : lavaan WARNING: sample covariance can not be\r<br>&gt; inverted\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Look at this:\r<br>\r<br> &gt; cor(Abun2[,c(&quot;Sc201_Stock&quot;,&quot;Sc202_Stock&quot;,&quot;Sc203_Stock&quot;,&quot;Sc210_Stock&quot;)])\r<br>             Sc201_Stock Sc202_Stock Sc203_Stock Sc210_Stock\r<br>Sc201_Stock   1.0000000   0.9954023   0.9933993   0.9607689\r<br>Sc202_Stock   0.9954023   1.0000000   0.9998189   0.9829169\r<br>Sc203_Stock   0.9933993   0.9998189   1.0000000   0.9862414\r<br>Sc210_Stock   0.9607689   0.9829169   0.9862414   1.0000000\r<br>\r<br>and then\r<br>\r<br> &gt; \r<br>eigen(cor(Abun2[,c(&quot;Sc201_Stock&quot;,&quot;Sc202_Stock&quot;,&quot;Sc203_Stock&quot;,&quot;Sc210_Stock&quot;)]))$values\r<br>[1]  3.959383e+00  4.061738e-02 -9.020562e-17 -5.133578e-16\r<br>\r<br>There is too much overlap among these 4 variables. You need to capture \r<br>the common information in one (two at the most) variables.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; Warning message: In lav_data_full(data = data, group = group,\r<br>&gt; group.label = group.label, : lavaan WARNING: unordered factor(s) with\r<br>&gt; more than 2 levels detected in data: BugTreat\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "BugTreat is a factor (with 3 levels). lavaan (unlike lm, glm) does not \r<br>automatically expand factors to a set of dummy variables. You have to do \r<br>that manually.\r<br>\r<br>For example:\r<br>\r<br>Abun2$BugTreat1 &lt;- ifelse(Abun2$BugTreat == &quot;Immigration&quot;, 1, 0)\r<br>Abun2$BugTreat2 &lt;- ifelse(Abun2$BugTreat == &quot;Initial&quot;, 1, 0)\r<br>\r<br>and then you replace &#39;BugTreat&#39; in your model syntax by those two dummy \r<br>variables:\r<br>\r<br>modbb &lt;- &#39;Sc200_FinalAbun ~ Sc200_Stock + BugTreat1 + BugTreat2 +  TempTreat\r<br>            Sc201_FinalAbun ~ Sc201_Stock + BugTreat1 + BugTreat2 + \r<br>TempTreat\r<br>            Sc202_FinalAbun ~ Sc202_Stock + BugTreat1 + BugTreat2 + \r<br>TempTreat\r<br>            Sc203_FinalAbun ~ Sc203_Stock + BugTreat1 + BugTreat2 + \r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "TempTreat\r<br>            Sc210_FinalAbun ~ Sc210_Stock +  TempTreat\r<br>            Sc211_FinalAbun ~ Sc211_Stock +  TempTreat &#39;\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "This works, but you still have to deal with the *_Stock variables.\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
