   "id": "NoKPjdcjz6sJ",
   "from": "rachael...@gmail.com",
   "author": "4ef440509a20f254",
   "date": "2014-07-03T21:43:47Z",
   "subject": "Re: error messages re: inversion of covariance, logl.H1, and factors with more than 2 levels",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Yves! <br>Your suggestions helped me resolve the issue with the 3-level factor BugTreat by splitting it into two 2-level columns.   <br><br>I&#39;m still working on how to reduce the number of *_Stock columns while retaining the info I need in the model.<br><br>Any idea about the third error?  I still get this error even if the model doesn&#39;t produce any other errors. <br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Error in fitMeasures(object, fit.measures = &quot;default&quot;) : \n object &#39;logl.H1&#39; not found<br><br><br></div>"
