   "subject": "Re: error messages re: inversion of covariance, logl.H1, and factors with more than 2 levels",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On 07/03/2014 11:43 PM, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rachael...@gmail.com</a> wrote:\r<br>&gt; Any idea about the third error?  I still get this error even if the\r<br>&gt; model doesn&#39;t produce any other errors.\r<br>&gt; Error in fitMeasures(object, fit.measures = &quot;default&quot;) : object\r<br>&gt; &#39;logl.H1&#39; not found\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "I did not see this with the model/data you posted.\r<br>\r<br>The error is only triggered (in lavaan 0.5-16) if some columns in your \r<br>data.frame are of type &#39;matrix&#39; (instead of numeric/integer/factor)...\r<br>\r<br>If your data.frame is called &#39;Data&#39;, and the variables in your model are \r<br>(say), &#39;x1&#39;, &#39;x2&#39;, &#39;x3&#39;, type\r<br>\r<br>varTable(Data[,c(&quot;x1&quot;,&quot;x2&quot;,&quot;x3&quot;)])\r<br>\r<br>In the &#39;type&#39; column: identify the variables that are of type &#39;matrix&#39;. \r<br>And make them numeric. For example, if &quot;x3&quot; is of type matrix:\r<br>\r<br>Data$x3 &lt;- as.numeric(Data$x3)\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "qGe9EeoUuOkJ",
