    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br><br><br>On Friday, July 4, 2014 1:38:43 AM UTC-5, Yves Rosseel wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">On 07/03/2014 11:43 PM, <a rel=\"nofollow\">rachael...@gmail.com</a> wrote:\n<br>&gt; Any idea about the third error?  I still get this error even if the\n<br>&gt; model doesn&#39;t produce any other errors.\n<br>&gt; Error in fitMeasures(object, fit.measures = &quot;default&quot;) : object\n<br>&gt; &#39;logl.H1&#39; not found\n<br>\n<br>I did not see this with the model/data you posted.\n<br>\n<br>The error is only triggered (in lavaan 0.5-16) if some columns in your \n<br>data.frame are of type &#39;matrix&#39; (instead of numeric/integer/factor)...\n<br>\n<br>If your data.frame is called &#39;Data&#39;, and the variables in your model are \n<br>(say), &#39;x1&#39;, &#39;x2&#39;, &#39;x3&#39;, type\n<br>\n<br>varTable(Data[,c(&quot;x1&quot;,&quot;x2&quot;,&quot;x3&quot;)])\n<br>\n<br>In the &#39;type&#39; column: identify the variables that are of type &#39;matrix&#39;. \n<br>And make them numeric. For example, if &quot;x3&quot; is of type matrix:\n<br>\n<br>Data$x3 &lt;- as.numeric(Data$x3)\n<br>\n<br>Yves.\n<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<br></blockquote></div>"
